metery of Ponta Delgada","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.733861,"lo":-25.687833,"d":1919,"ds":"The Jewish Cemetery of Ponta Delgada is a Jewish cemetery located in Ponta Delgada, Azores. Here is buried Mimom ben Abraham Abohbot, founder of the Synagogue Ets Haim in Angra do Heroísmo.","wpu":"Jewish cemetery of Ponta Delgada","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Cemiterio_judaico_pta_delgada_%281%29.jpg/960px-Cemiterio_judaico_pta_delgada_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Church of Santa Cruz (Lagoa)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.743161,"lo":-25.56515,"d":8967,"ds":"The Church of Santa Cruz (Portuguese: Igreja de Santa Cruz) is a Catholic church situated in the civil parish of Santa Cruz, in the municipality of Lagoa, in the Portuguese archipelago of the Azores.","wpu":"Church of Santa Cruz (Lagoa)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/SMG_LAG_Nsr_SantaCruz2.jpg/960px-SMG_LAG_Nsr_SantaCruz2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Ponta Delgada (European Portuguese pronunciation: [ˈpõtɐ ðɛlˈɣaðɐ] ; lit. 'Thin Cape') is the largest municipality (concelho) and executive capital of the Autonomous Region of the Azores in Portugal. It is located on São Miguel Island, the largest and most populous in the archipelago. As of 2021, it has 67,287 inhabitants, in an area of 232.99 square kilometres (89.96 square miles).","wpu":"Ponta Delgada","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Ayuntamiento%2C_Ponta_Delgada%2C_isla_de_San_Miguel%2C_Azores%2C_Portugal%2C_2020-07-29%2C_DD_126-128_HDR.jpg/960px-Ayuntamiento%2C_Ponta_Delgada%2C_isla_de_San_Miguel%2C_Azores%2C_Portugal%2C_2020-07-29%2C_DD_126-128_HDR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}